// cases_canvas.cla: Canvas (Task 7, ui-scenario-retirement batch) -- the
// migrated replacement for the retired testdata/ui/canvas.cla golden UI
// scenario: a buffered canvas animated by a top-level `every 4 ticks`
// block (a 20x20 filled square sliding right), asserted by the retired
// suite purely as "two snaps taken after different amounts of ticking
// differ" (internal/mactest/ui_test.go's own checkCanvasSnaps, no other
// Go-side invariant, confirmed before writing this case). See harness.
// cla's own CanvasWin comment for the window/every-block transcription
// (unchanged cadence: `every 4 ticks`, same dx=3 step).
//
// UiTestTick(n)'s scripted-mode path forwards to the SAME "tick n" verb
// (rtUiScriptDispatchLine -> rtUiScriptTick, uiscript.cla) a `.events`
// script line would dispatch -- there is no separate "test-mode" every-
// pump logic, so a window opened MID-CASE (this case runs inside
// RunAll's own dispatch, not at App.launch like the retired fixture's own
// `on App.launch { open Anim }`) still gets its `every` block pumped
// correctly: rtUiScriptEveryPump (uiscript.cla) iterates the global
// rtUiEveryDueArr and fires whatever's due purely by elapsed virtual-tick
// count, with no dependency on which window is frontmost or when it was
// opened. `CanvasWin.front` (the every-block's own guard) is "the
// frontmost OPEN INSTANCE of type CanvasWin" (language reference: "Doc.
// front is the frontmost open instance of type Doc"), not "the frontmost
// window overall" -- so it resolves correctly even while this suite's own
// Suite window is the actual frontmost window on screen throughout.
//
// FIXED RUNTIME BUG (native-gaps-cleanup Task 6; formerly a discovered-
// and-worked-around quirk, see task-7-report.md's own "concerns" section
// for the original escalation and misdiagnosis): this case used to need a
// large warm-up `UiTestTick` call before the real measured cadence because
// this suite's own composed build measured the every-block's INITIAL `due`
// tick as `50`, not the expected `4`.
//
// Root-caused (not guessed -- a temporary debug probe recorded
// `peekb(UiTestScript())` and the seeded `now` at the exact moment
// `rtUiBuildEvery` ran, then a case read them back): `rtUiBuildEvery`'s own
// `peekb(UiTestScript()) != 0` seed was ALREADY correct every time (reads
// nonzero, seeds `now = 0`, due = `0 + 4` = `4`) -- the real bug was
// `rtUiEveryPump` (ui.cla), the ONE every-array reader/writer that did NOT
// gate on `rtUiScripted` the way its virtual-tick twin
// (`rtUiScriptEveryPump`, uiscript.cla), `UiTestTick`, `rtUiRun`, and
// `rtUiLaunch` all do. `testsuite/toolbox/cases_uitest.cla`'s
// `casePostEventClick` (an EARLIER-dispatched case, by design driving the
// REAL event loop to deliver a real `PostEvent`-queued click) legitimately
// calls `rtUiEveryPump()` directly to replicate a real loop iteration's
// idle work -- but that pump is program-wide, not scoped to whichever
// window is open, so its real-`UiTickCount()`-based reschedule (`due = now
// + interval`, `now` ~46 that deep into this suite's own larger startup)
// stomped THIS case's still-unopened CanvasWin every-block's `due` from
// `4` to `50`, long before this case ever ran. Fixed at the source:
// `rtUiEveryPump` now forwards to `rtUiScriptEveryPump` whenever
// `rtUiScripted` is true, so every current and future caller of the real
// pump (not just this one) gets the virtual-tick-consistent behavior for
// free. See `rtUiEveryPump`'s own doc comment (ui.cla) for the full
// mechanism.
//
// With the fix, `due` starts at the correctly-seeded `4` and this case
// needs no warm-up at all -- the geometry math below is UNCHANGED (it
// already excluded the old warm-up's own one-time bump from its own
// firing count), so this case is now both simpler AND the regression test
// for the fix: if `rtUiEveryPump` regresses to ignoring `rtUiScripted`
// again, `casePostEventClick`'s own earlier real-pump call would once
// again stomp `due` with a real-tick value, this case's un-warmed cadence
// would no longer land the square where expected, and `s1 == s2` would
// FAIL.
//
// A tick's every-pump fires each due entry AT MOST ONCE per UiTestTick
// call, regardless of the `n` passed (same "at most once per tick N
// script line" contract canvas.events' own header comment documents) --
// so this case calls UiTestTick(4) three times (not UiTestTick(12) once)
// to get three firings before the first checksum, mirroring canvas.events'
// own "tick 4" x3 cadence exactly, then five more calls before the second
// checksum (canvas.events' own "tick 4" x5).

// tbCanvasCkX0/Y0/W/H: an 8px-aligned checksum region that fully contains
// the sliding square at BOTH sampled positions. CanvasWin's `size: 160,
// 160` -> content top-left ((512-160)/2, 44) = (176, 44) (already a
// multiple of 8, no local-offset adjustment needed). The square is a
// 20x20 fill at LOCAL (x, 60); x is 19 after 3 firings (10 + 3*3) and 34
// after 8 firings (19 + 3*5) -- see this file's own header comment. LOCAL
// x=16 (176+16=192, a multiple of 8) through LOCAL x=56 (176+56=232, a
// multiple of 8, width 40) fully
// contains both squares' bounding boxes (19..39 and 34..54, both inside
// [16,56]) with margin on every side.
const tbCanvasCkX0: int = 192
const tbCanvasCkY0: int = 104
const tbCanvasCkW: int = 40
const tbCanvasCkH: int = 20

func caseCanvas(): TestResult {
    var w: CanvasWin
    var i: int
    var s1: int
    var s2: int
    var detail: string

    w = open CanvasWin

    i = 0
    while i < 3 {
        UiTestTick(4)
        i = i + 1
    }
    s1 = UiTestChecksum(tbCanvasCkX0, tbCanvasCkY0, tbCanvasCkW, tbCanvasCkH)

    i = 0
    while i < 5 {
        UiTestTick(4)
        i = i + 1
    }
    s2 = UiTestChecksum(tbCanvasCkX0, tbCanvasCkY0, tbCanvasCkW, tbCanvasCkH)

    close w

    if s1 != s2 {
        return tkPass("Canvas")
    }
    detail = "s1 " + tkIntToStr(s1) + " == s2 " + tkIntToStr(s2)
    return tkFail("Canvas", detail)
}
